A continuation marker attaches one block, and the boundary is that block's extent

```
- a
+
para
> q
.
<ul>
  <li>a
    para
&gt; q
  </li>
</ul>
```

```
- a
+
para
+
> q
.
<ul>
  <li>a
    para
    <blockquote><p>q</p></blockquote>
  </li>
</ul>
```

```
- a
+
p1
p2
> q
.
<ul>
  <li>a
    p1
p2
&gt; q
  </li>
</ul>
```

```
- a
+
> x
> y
- next
.
<ul>
  <li>a
    <blockquote><p>x
y</p></blockquote>
  </li>
  <li>next</li>
</ul>
```

```
- a
+
- x
- y
.
<ul>
  <li>a</li>
  <li>x</li>
  <li>y</li>
</ul>
```

